From: Stained Glass OS <ke7oxh@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] dmscript: the script track loads its events, runs their routines in Play, Clone / PlayEx / GetParamEx / SetParamEx

The script track of dmscript returned S_OK from Init, InitPlay, EndPlay,
Play, Clone, PlayEx, GetParamEx, SetParamEx and Load without looking at its
arguments. It now:

- Load: reads the 'scrt' list (events 'scre' with header 'scrh', the
  routine name 'scrn' and the 'DMRF' reference of the script, which is
  fetched through the loader of the stream); E_POINTER without a stream,
  DMUS_E_UNSUPPORTED_STREAM for another list or an event without header,
  name or script.
- Init: E_POINTER without segment. InitPlay: E_POINTER without segment
  state, performance or state data; initialises the scripts of the events
  for the performance and returns a play state. EndPlay: E_POINTER without
  state, frees it.
- Play: E_POINTER without state or performance; calls the routine of every
  event whose time lies in [start, end) and returns the first routine
  failure (DMUS_E_SCRIPT_ERROR_IN_SCRIPT). The PREPARE, QUEUE and ATTIME
  timings of an event are all served when its range is played.
- PlayEx: E_POINTER without performance, converts the reference times
  through the performance and plays.
- Clone: E_POINTER without result, E_INVALIDARG for a negative or inverted
  range, a new track with the events of the range moved to start at zero
  (sharing the scripts).
- GetParamEx / SetParamEx: the track has no parameters, so
  DMUS_E_GET_UNSUPPORTED / DMUS_E_SET_UNSUPPORTED like GetParam/SetParam.
- AddNotificationType, RemoveNotificationType, Compose, Join, Save and
  GetSizeMax stay E_NOTIMPL (the conformance test asserts that).

Conformance test: the todo_wine marks on Init, InitPlay, EndPlay, Play
(E_POINTER), Clone(NULL) and PlayEx(NULL) are removed.
Test: test/dmscript-gate.sh (+ dmscript-probe.c).
